\section{Formal Proof of Convergence and Boundedness}

Let the full CMD state be
\[
\mathbf{\Psi}(t) =
\begin{bmatrix}
\mathbf{q}(t) \\
\mathbf{p}(t)
\end{bmatrix},
\]
where $\mathbf{q}$ includes SPH particle distributions, viscoelastic tensor fields, and immune state-machine matrices, and $\mathbf{p}$ denotes canonical momenta.

\subsection{Theorem 1 (Global Invariant Boundedness under Astrophysical Forcing)}

\textit{
Given bounded astrophysical forcing $\|\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{astro}}(t)\| \le M_{\mathrm{astro}}$ and strictly positive dissipation $\gamma > 0$, the trajectory $\mathbf{\Psi}(t)$ remains permanently confined within a compact, globally attractive invariant set $\mathcal{B} \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ for all $t \ge 0$.
}

\subsubsection{Proof}

Define the Lyapunov candidate:
\[
V(\mathbf{\Psi}) = \mathcal{H}(\mathbf{q},\mathbf{p}) + V_{\mathrm{Lyap}}(\mathbf{q}),
\]
which is positive definite and radially unbounded.

Taking the derivative along system trajectories:
\[
\frac{dV}{dt}
\le
- \gamma \|\delta\mathbf{q}\|^2
+ c_1 \|\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{astro}}(t)\|,
\qquad
\|\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{astro}}(t)\| \le M_{\mathrm{astro}}.
\]

Choosing $\gamma$ to dominate the Lipschitz growth bound yields:
\[
\frac{dV}{dt} \le -\alpha V + M_{\mathrm{astro}},
\qquad \alpha > 0.
\]

Applying Grönwall’s inequality:
\[
V(t) \le V(0)e^{-\alpha t} + \frac{M_{\mathrm{astro}}}{\alpha}.
\]

Thus,
\[
\|\mathbf{\Psi}(t)\|
\le
\sqrt{\frac{M_{\mathrm{astro}}}{\alpha c_1}}
\quad \text{as } t \to \infty,
\]
establishing the invariant bounded set
\[
\mathcal{B}
=
\left\{
\mathbf{\Psi} \;\middle|\;
\|\mathbf{\Psi}\| \le
\sqrt{\frac{M_{\mathrm{astro}}}{\alpha c_1}}
\right\}.
\qquad \blacksquare
\]

